// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/queen/task_tree_check.t27 -- full-chain verification matrix for the task tree and its
; return protocol. CHECKS track, task-10 (branch spec/zoom-checks).
; 
; This spec is the acceptance layer of the delegation slice (task-7 model law, task-8 runtime).
; It exercises the model + runtime through their PUBLIC functions only: specs/queen/task_tree.t27
; (task tree: parent links, attempts, states), specs/queen/actors.t27 (return protocol tags,
; scope subset), specs/queen/events.t27 (EV_RESULT / EV_ACCEPTED kinds), and the aggregation in
; specs/queen/actor_events.t27 (envelope: seq / at / from_pid / to_pid / task_ref).
; It does NOT restate or re-derive any law; a rule tested here is owned by the file that
; defines it. Contract tests for functions a task-7/8 file itself owns live with that file.
; 
; The ten cases of the verification matrix (one test name each, section 2 below):
;   1  multiple branches and nested levels
;   2  result returned along the correct parent link
;   3  repeated delivery without double completion (idempotent result delivery)
;   4  stale result from a previous attempt
;   5  executor disappearance and restart
;   6  parent cancel with a running child
;   7  budget exhaustion
;   8  one-branch error without a false global completion
;   9  history preserved across an executor change
;  10  no privilege escalation on delegation (child rights are a subset of the passed scope)
; 
; Status 2026-11-01 (3): engine asserts landed (delegate_runtime.t27, spec/integration):
; case 6 cancel (dr_cancel_ok), case 7 budget (dr_admit/DR_ADMIT_BUDGET), engine redelivery
; (dr_deliver_ok/dr_redelivery_refused), verdicts (dr_verdict_ok), and the shell_state legs
; (ss_tab_switch_keeps_sel / ss_viewport_keep / ss_back) fill the scenario and bridge TODOs.
; All CONTRACT MODE: engine/shell functions with fixture states; the executable host call is
; held for the owner. One test stays vacuous by design: case 8 (one-branch aggregation) waits
; for task-8's aggregation. Earlier status:
; Status 2026-11-01 (2): model-law asserts landed (cases 1-4, model halves of 5/9/10); the
; full-chain scenario lives in section 3 in CONTRACT MODE -- every step asserts a landed law
; (t27os zoom law, t27f viz contract, task-tree law), runtime-dependent legs are named TODOs
; keyed to task-8/12/13; section 4 is the QLG_Z <-> VIZ_ bridge: keep/gone/back mean the same
; on both sides, by semantics and never by numeric constants. Still TODO: real-call halves
; (case 5 restart, 6 cancel-with-running-child, 7 budget exhaustion mid-run, 8 aggregation,
; 9 event-seq ordering, the section-3 runtime evidence) land after task-8. Fixtures only in
; sections 2-4; nothing passes vacuously.
; 
; Fixtures vs real calls: transformation tests in section 2 use fixtures built from the model
; functions; the integration scenario (section 3) uses real calls through the runtime. The two
; are never mixed in one claim.
; ASCII only (L3). L4: every rule named above has a test block in this file.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

